# Testing Rules

## Backend (`tests/Backend/`)

- `PTS.Architecture.Tests` mechanically enforces module boundaries (see
  `00-modular-monolith-architecture.mdc`) via reflection over compiled
  assemblies — no third-party architecture-testing library is used unless a
  documented need arises (per the "don't add dependencies speculatively" rule).
  **Do not weaken or delete these tests to make a boundary violation pass** —
  fix the dependency direction instead.
- Once tenant-owned tables/RLS policies exist, add integration tests that prove:
  a query executed under `app_role` with tenant context A cannot read/write rows
  belonging to tenant B, even if application code forgets a `WHERE TenantId = ...`
  clause. This is the concrete test of the "RLS is mandatory, app filtering alone
  is not sufficient" rule.
- Unit tests for a module belong under a `PTS.Modules.<Name>.Tests` project once
  that module has real behavior to test — don't create empty test projects ahead
  of implementation.

## Frontend (`src/Web/`)

- Use `vitest` (already configured in `vite.config.ts`). Run with `npm run test`.
- Pure localization/utility logic (e.g. `src/i18n/direction.ts`) must have unit
  tests colocated as `*.test.ts` next to the source file.
- Do not snapshot-test translated strings directly (they will legitimately change
  per locale); test behavior (e.g. "Arabic resolves to rtl"), not exact copy.

## General

- Don't claim a test "passes" without having actually run it in this workspace.
  If something can't be verified yet (e.g. no database is running), say so
  explicitly rather than assuming success.
